IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ia-time`

-- Interpretation Act 1965, ss 2, 50, 51 -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked
-- against a decided case or subsidiary legislation (none was retrieved).
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table of which flags are set (scratchpad gen_interpretation-act.py). Expected results were written by
-- hand from the text.

-- Day numbers: day 0 is Monday 1 January 2024 (see ia-time.l4). The two holiday calendars are test fixtures, not the real
-- Singapore calendar: one with no public holidays, one treating Mon 8 and Tue 9 January 2024 (days 7, 8) as public holidays,
-- and one treating Mon 15 January (day 14) as a public holiday.

§ `Fixtures`

`no public holidays` MEANS Calendar WITH
    `public holiday one` IS 999999
    `public holiday two` IS 999999
    `public holiday three` IS 999999

`holidays on 8 and 9 January` MEANS Calendar WITH
    `public holiday one` IS 7
    `public holiday two` IS 8
    `public holiday three` IS 999999

`a holiday on 15 January` MEANS Calendar WITH
    `public holiday one` IS 14
    `public holiday two` IS 999999
    `public holiday three` IS 999999

§ `s 2`

#ASSERT `what a month is`  EQUALS "a calendar month"

#ASSERT `what a year is`  EQUALS "a year reckoned according to the Gregorian calendar"

§ `s 50 -- excluded days`

#ASSERT `day is a Sunday` 6
#ASSERT `day is a Sunday` 13
#ASSERT NOT `day is a Sunday` 5
#ASSERT NOT `day is a Sunday` 0

#ASSERT `day is excluded in` 6 `no public holidays`
#ASSERT NOT `day is excluded in` 5 `no public holidays`
#ASSERT `day is excluded in` 7 `holidays on 8 and 9 January`
#ASSERT NOT `day is excluded in` 7 `no public holidays`

#ASSERT `first day not excluded from` 6 `no public holidays` EQUALS 7
#ASSERT `first day not excluded from` 6 `holidays on 8 and 9 January` EQUALS 9
#ASSERT `first day not excluded from` 5 `no public holidays` EQUALS 5

§ `s 50(a), (b) -- periods over 6 days`

#ASSERT `last day of a period of days` 10 0 `no public holidays` EQUALS 10
#ASSERT `last day of a period of days` 13 0 `no public holidays` EQUALS 14
#ASSERT `last day of a period of days` 13 0 `a holiday on 15 January` EQUALS 15
#ASSERT `last day of a period of days` 7 0 `no public holidays` EQUALS 7

§ `s 50(d) -- periods of 6 days or less`

#ASSERT `last day of a period of days` 3 4 `no public holidays` EQUALS 8
#ASSERT `last day of a period of days` 3 4 `holidays on 8 and 9 January` EQUALS 10
#ASSERT `last day of a period of days` 6 0 `no public holidays` EQUALS 7
#ASSERT `last day of a period of days` 1 5 `no public holidays` EQUALS 7

§ `s 50(c) -- acts on a fixed day`

#ASSERT `act on a fixed day is in due time` 6 7 `no public holidays`
#ASSERT NOT `act on a fixed day is in due time` 6 8 `no public holidays`
#ASSERT `act on a fixed day is in due time` 5 5 `no public holidays`
#ASSERT NOT `act on a fixed day is in due time` 5 7 `no public holidays`
#ASSERT `act on a fixed day is in due time` 6 9 `holidays on 8 and 9 January`

§ `s 51`

#ASSERT `standard time hours ahead of UTC`  EQUALS 8

§ `Attaining an age`

#ASSERT NOT `this Act fixes when a person attains an age` 

